# Shell scripts always run on Linux (the Pi appliance, or a Linux dev
# machine) regardless of which OS checked this repo out. Found live,
# 2026-09-06: this Windows checkout's `core.autocrlf=true`, with no
# override, had silently rewritten several already-deployed scripts to
# CRLF -- `set -uo pipefail` becomes an "invalid option name" the moment
# the last option on the line carries a trailing `\r`, and a bare `\r` on
# its own line becomes "command not found". Several `build/*.sh` scripts
# had already been running this way all session, tolerated by luck (no
# fragile-enough construct on an early line) rather than correctness --
# not something to keep depending on.
#
# `text eol=lf` forces LF on checkout AND on commit, independent of
# whatever `core.autocrlf` a given clone has set, so this cannot recur on
# a different machine either.
*.sh            text eol=lf
LempiPi/lempi-*    text eol=lf

# The same argument, for the files systemd and its neighbours read. Every
# `.service`, `.timer` and `.conf` in this tree is consumed on the Pi and
# nowhere else: systemd drop-ins, mpd configs, pipewire and tmpfiles
# fragments. Checked 2026-09-21 and every one of them was already CRLF in a
# Windows checkout, having been committed without a rule -- systemd happens
# to strip the trailing carriage return, which is why nothing had broken and
# why nobody had noticed. That is tolerance, not correctness, and it is not
# shared by everything else that reads these files.
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf

# The same argument again, for Linux-consumed files the patterns above miss
# because they carry no extension at all, or one nobody thought to name.
# Added 2026-09-21 after an audit: the shell test runner and its seven stubs
# are executed by `LempiPi/tests/run` on a Linux box, a `\r` inside a
# `RUN`/`ENTRYPOINT` line breaks a Docker build the same way it breaks a
# shell, and `targets.env` is *parsed* -- `build/lib-defaults.sh` reads a
# value out of it with `${_line#*=}`, which keeps a trailing carriage return
# and hands `pi@speaker-a\r` to ssh. The index already held LF for all of
# them; only a Windows checkout saw CRLF, which is the hardest version of
# this bug to see from the machine that has it.
LempiPi/tests/run       text eol=lf
LempiPi/tests/stubs/*   text eol=lf
build/Dockerfile.*      text eol=lf
*.env                   text eol=lf
